            Buying Tip
          </p>
          <p class="text-amber-800 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Before paying for a used C 990, read the model number off the decal and get the manual
            for that number. Ask the seller to run the incline calibration from the maintenance
            mode, do the manual's lift test (each belt edge should lift 2 to 3 inches off the
            platform), and walk and jog on it to check the belt does not slip or drift. Remember
            that the original warranty does not pass to you.
