        <div id="who-should-skip" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Who Should Skip This Treadmill</h2>
        <p>
          Skip a used C 990 if you want a warranty: the original cover was for the first owner
          only, and a new
          <a href="/nordictrack-t-series-treadmill/">T Series 10</a> gives you the same belt,
          incline and speed with one. Skip it if you run regularly at faster paces, because the
          <a href="/nordictrack-commercial-1250-treadmill/">Commercial 1250</a> or
          <a href="/nordictrack-commercial-1750-treadmill/">Commercial 1750</a> offer more motor
          headroom and a wider belt. Skip it if you are near 300 lb, since sources disagree on its
          capacity. And if you know you will never pay for iFit, a simpler non-connected treadmill
          from our
          <a href="/best-treadmill-under-1000-reviews/">budget treadmill guide</a>
          may suit you better than an aging connected console.
        </p>
        </div>

        <div id="verdict" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">10. Final Verdict</h2>
        <p>
          The NordicTrack C 990 was an honest entry-level treadmill, and on paper its 20 x 60-inch
          belt, 0 to 12% incline and 12 mph top speed still match NordicTrack's cheapest current
          model. But it is no longer sold new, its 7-inch console dates from around 2015, and its
          warranty does not transfer. For walkers and joggers who find a well-kept one at a low
          price, it remains a sensible machine.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are weighing a used C 990 against something new, be honest about the price gap.
          A small saving on a T Series 10 is not worth giving up a warranty for. A large one can
          be, provided the machine passes the <a href="/treadmill-calibration/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>incline calibration</a>, the belt lift test and a few
          minutes of walking and jogging before you take it home.
        </p>
