        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">11. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the NordicTrack C 990 good for running, or just walking?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              It suits walking, incline walking and jogging best. Independent listings give it a 20 x 60-inch belt, 0 to 12% incline and a 12 mph top speed, so the belt is a running length; the limits are a 3.0 CHP motor rating and the age of the machine, which is no longer sold new. Regular faster runners will get more headroom from a current Commercial 1250 or 1750.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How does the C 990 compare to the C 1650?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Both are older C-Series models that are no longer on NordicTrack's US site. Independent reviews give both a 20 x 60-inch belt, 0 to 12% incline and a 12 mph top speed; the C 1650 adds a 10-inch touchscreen in place of 7 inches and a higher motor rating, listed at 3.5 CHP against 3.0. Buying either means buying used, so the condition of the individual machine matters more than the difference between the two models.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I have to pay for iFit to use the C 990?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              No. The manual mode and the console's onboard workouts run without a membership. iFit workouts, including trainer-led automatic speed and incline changes, need a Wi-Fi connection and a paid membership, and a used C 990 will not come with the membership that was included when it was new. Ask iFIT whether a console of this age is still supported before you pay for one.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the C 990's deck too small for taller users?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Probably not for walking or jogging. Independent listings give a 20 x 60-inch belt, the same length as NordicTrack's current Commercial models and two inches narrower. Sixty inches is a common running length, so taller users are more likely to notice the narrower belt and the 3.0 CHP motor rating than the length. Walk and jog on a used one before you buy it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How loud is the C 990 at higher speeds?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              We have not measured it. As a general rule a lower-rated motor works harder at a given speed than a higher-rated one, so expect more motor noise during sustained running than on NordicTrack's Commercial models and less difference at walking pace. On a used machine extra noise can also come from a worn belt or loose parts, so listen to it running before you buy.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does assembly take?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              The manual gives no time, but it says assembly requires two persons and uses the included hex keys and a Phillips screwdriver, with no power tools. A second person is called for again to hold the console and the frame in later steps. A used C 990 will usually arrive assembled; the manual notes that moving it may require two people and that you must be able to lift 45 lb safely to fold or move it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Where can I find the NordicTrack C 990 manual?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Start with the full model number on the serial decal on the frame. The US manual we read is for NTL19815.0, and parts catalogs list revisions up to NTL19815.8 plus NETL numbers sold outside the US. As of October 20, 2026, NordicTrack's US site sends support visitors to iFIT's Member Center at my.ifit.com, and Customer Service is 1-833-680-4348. The manual covers assembly, belt tension and centring, troubleshooting by symptom and the limited warranty. It gives no lubrication interval and says not to add lubricant unless a service representative tells you to.
            </p>
