      <!-- Common Mistakes -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buyers Make</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Buying a C 990 now means buying a discontinued machine second-hand, and most regret comes from treating it like a new one. Watch for these four.</p>
        <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming the warranty comes with it</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The C 990's lifetime frame and motor cover applied to the original purchaser only, according to the manual. Price a second-hand machine as if it has no warranty, because it almost certainly does not.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying close to new-machine money</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">NordicTrack listed the T Series 10, with the same belt, incline and top speed plus a 10-inch screen and a current warranty, at $1,599.99 on 14 October 2026. A used C 990 has to be priced well below that to make sense.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming iFit comes with it</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The included membership was for new buyers. A used C 990 needs its own paid iFit membership for trainer-led workouts, and its console has to still be supported. Without one, plan to use the manual mode and onboard workouts.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring folded height before collection</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The C 990 folds upward, so the constraint is ceiling and doorway clearance, not floor area. The manual does not give a folded size, so measure the machine folded before you move it, not after it is stuck in a stairwell.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
